# Bead ids whose "declared complete by a commit" signal is known to be WRONG.
#
# .claude/hooks/check-beads.sh treats a bead id alone on a line in a commit
# message as "this commit finished it". That convention is real and it found a
# genuine miss (news-brief-bqa.12, built in d48b036 and left open for a day).
# But a trailer can name the wrong bead, and history cannot be rewritten once
# pushed -- so the mis-attribution has to be recorded here instead.
#
# Only add an id after establishing that the COMMIT is wrong, not the bead.
# An id listed here is invisible to signal 1 forever; if the bead is genuinely
# finished later, close it rather than relying on the hook to notice.

# Commit 338d2bb ("opaque candidate labels, so an invented id cannot collide")
# ends with this id, but bqa.11 is "Enable COMPREHEND_ENABLED in production and
# run the pre-registered gate" -- blocked on bqa.19 and not started. The label
# work it actually describes had no bead of its own. The bead status is right;
# the trailer is wrong.
news-brief-bqa.11
